 "relevance_note": "Single case report of a 69-year-old man whose past medical history includes \"Tangier's disease\"; he is in scope by diagnosis, but the paper names no ABCA1 variant, gene or genetic test.",
 "method_note": "Single case report; one in-scope person (label 'patient', rule 5). Tangier disease appears only as an item in the past medical history; no gene, variant, genetic testing, lipid values or Tangier-specific findings are given, so the variants table is empty (the paper ties no ABCA1 variant to the person) and the diagnosis basis is not reported. Built with a short Python script from my own reading; spans checked verbatim by script. Age 69 years is recorded as age at last evaluation (age at this admission). Vital status left not reported: the paper reports completion of antibiotics before discharge but does not state vital status. Checklist: only coronary artery disease observed. Abdominal aortic aneurysm with endograft is recorded as a feature but not as 'non-coronary atherosclerotic arterial disease', because the paper does not call this patient's aneurysm atherosclerotic (the Discussion speaks of 'patients with atherosclerotic abdominal aortic disease' in general, 'As this case demonstrates'). Type 2 diabetes mellitus is recorded as a feature but the checklist item 'glucose intolerance or impaired insulin secretion' is left not reported, as the paper does not state either. CT of head, chest and abdomen/pelvis on admission was 'unremarkable' (a whole investigation; excludes nothing specific, so no row). Echocardiograms negative for intracardiac lesions/abscesses recorded as excluded with the paper's wording. No contradictions found.",
